{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts | sed -n '98,138p'\"","aggregated_output":"    98\tconst DEFAULT_LHC_DIR = join(homedir(), \".lhc\");\n    99\t\n   100\t/** The Story-1 production inference placeholder: a real `DerivationProvider`\n   101\t *  whose every operation fails closed (non-retryable) instead of fabricating a\n   102\t *  derived form. Epic 1 is observe-only and Story 1 does not capture yet\n   103\t *  (message_end is a no-op until Story 2) and lands no work handlers, so no\n   104\t *  derivation work is ever queued and this provider is never invoked — it exists\n   105\t *  only to satisfy SDK construction (AC-1.1 \"initializes one LHC instance\").\n   106\t *\n   107\t *  It is deliberately NOT the deterministic provider, which the LHC SDK\n   108\t *  documents as \"selectable only by explicit name — never a production default\"\n   109\t *  (it would mark fake derived text into the thread). Failing closed preserves\n   110\t *  the observe-only guarantee even if a future change queued work before Stories\n   111\t *  5/6 wire the real PI-model-registry-backed inference config (`ModelCall` +\n   112\t *  assignments), which is what a real *completing* inference requires (the\n   113\t *  `@earendil-works/pi-ai` completion package is not yet a build dependency). */\n   114\tfunction observeOnlyProvider(): DerivationProvider {\n   115\t  const notConfigured = (): Promise<ProviderResult> =>\n   116\t    Promise.resolve({\n   117\t      ok: false,\n   118\t      retryable: false,\n   119\t      reason: \"pi-lhc inference is not configured yet (Epic 1 Stories 5/6)\",\n   120\t    });\n   121\t  return {\n   122\t    smoothPrompt: notConfigured,\n   123\t    summarizeToolCall: notConfigured,\n   124\t    summarizeToolResult: notConfigured,\n   125\t    composeTurnRendering: notConfigured,\n   126\t    projectLowerBand: notConfigured,\n   127\t    summarizeChunkDetailed: notConfigured,\n   128\t    summarizeChunkBrief: notConfigured,\n   129\t  };\n   130\t}\n   131\t\n   132\t/** The production observe-only SDK config: a real, construction-valid instance\n   133\t *  in background scheduler mode, built on the fail-closed `observeOnlyProvider`\n   134\t *  above. Stories 5/6 replace this default with the PI-auth-backed inference\n   135\t *  config. */\n   136\tfunction defaultBuildSdkConfig(): OpResult<SdkConfig> {\n   137\t  return { ok: true, value: { provider: observeOnlyProvider(), mode: \"background\" } };\n   138\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
